# Small Staged Delivery

- When planning implementation work, split it into the smallest separate stages that are still functional and independently verifiable.
- Each stage should produce a coherent working state, not a partial broken checkpoint.
- After each stage, run the smallest relevant test/check that verifies that stage.
- Commit after each verified stage before starting the next one, unless the user explicitly asks not to commit.
- Keep stage scope narrow enough that failures are easy to isolate and commits remain reviewable.
